//@version=4
study("UCTPROBE_VW_A4_PARAM_BRANCH", overlay=false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-20 for the Pine parity programme, objects unit A4 (capture queue
// docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-20-a4-param-branch.md, Q-A4-2). NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW.
// The support-and-resistance shape: a branch of a function body decided by a parameter the call passes
// per bar, with history (`cum`, `a[p]`) in the arm. The runtime lane draws such a branch while it has run
// on every call (P01, C00) and stops by name at the first call it skips (P02). P02's reading is what Pine
// keeps over the calls the arm ran on (what serving it per run would have to equal).
//   P01  the per-bar parameter is never 1: the else arm runs on every call
//   P02  the parameter is 1 on bars 3, 10, 17, ...: the else arm skips those calls
//   C00  a fixed parameter (the call site fixes the branch)
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D from the listing, inputs at defaults; AMEX:SPY 1D second.

Sma(src,p) => a = cum(src), (a - a[max(p,0)])/max(p,0)
Variance(src,p) => p == 1 ? 0 : Sma(src*src,p) - pow(Sma(src,p),2)
k1 = bar_index > 10 ? 5 : 2
k2 = bar_index % 7 == 3 ? 1 : 5

plot(bar_index, title="A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(Variance(close, k1), title="P01_every_call")
plot(Variance(close, k2), title="P02_skips")
plot(Variance(close, 5), title="C00_fixed")
